From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Allow the program binary cache to be switched off

Add projectm_opengl_set_program_cache_enabled. Disabled, every shader program is
compiled and linked from source in the context that uses it: the binary-retrievable
hint is not set, no binary is exported or loaded with glProgramBinary, and cached
entries are dropped. Every driver binary call (hint, export, load) is admitted
only while the cache is enabled, and disabling waits for admitted calls on other
threads to finish, so none runs after the switch returns. Enabled again, the
cache starts empty. Default and enabled behaviour are unchanged.

TV-only diagnostic control: ProjectM TV exposes it as an Advanced setting to test
GPU drivers (first reported on a PowerVR GE9215 Fire TV Stick) whose program
binaries may fail when moved between EGL contexts. Not proposed upstream; the
program cache itself is TV-only (patch 0001).

---
diff --git a/src/api/include/projectM-4/render_opengl.h b/src/api/include/projectM-4/render_opengl.h
index 5d0f09f01..67f123478 100644
--- a/src/api/include/projectM-4/render_opengl.h
+++ b/src/api/include/projectM-4/render_opengl.h
@@ -74,6 +74,19 @@ PROJECTM_EXPORT void projectm_opengl_burn_texture(projectm_handle instance, uint
  */
 PROJECTM_EXPORT void projectm_opengl_program_cache_stats(uint32_t* hits, uint32_t* misses);
 
+/**
+ * @brief Enables (the default) or disables the process-wide cache of linked shader programs.
+ *
+ * Disabled, every program is compiled and linked from source in the context that uses it: no
+ * program binary is requested, exported or loaded with glProgramBinary, and cached entries are
+ * dropped. For drivers whose program binaries fail when moved between contexts. Thread-safe:
+ * disabling waits for binary calls already under way on other threads, so none runs after it
+ * returns; applies to programs compiled after the call.
+ *
+ * @param enabled true to cache program binaries, false to always compile.
+ */
+PROJECTM_EXPORT void projectm_opengl_set_program_cache_enabled(bool enabled);
+
 /**
  * @brief During a soft-cut transition, renders the outgoing preset only every n-th frame.
  *
